{{box title="Status of this page"}}
Draft. Objectives, Use Cases, Functions, Premises and Claims traceable to the Foundation.

* No primary data: no resident or care worker observed or interviewed.
* References cited from memory; checked in the evidence pass (Open item O-1).
* Cells marked [threshold - O-3] still need numbers.
{{/box}}

**Abstract.** Nine objectives, three use cases, six functions. UC01: the guided garden walk - the core. UC02: seated or lying practice - the rain-day and dusk complement. UC03: listening - radio, news, audiobooks. Six Premises verify that the Functions work; fourteen Claims, four of them adverse, test whether they help.

= Objectives =

== Objective - Walk more [OBJ-01] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-01
|Name|Walk more
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Goal on SA-01; PS-01, PS-02. Forbes et al. (2015); HFC-01 (hypothesis).
|Statement|Residents walk outdoors more often and for longer, and finish the walks they start.
|Type|Operational
|Derived from|Goal on SA-01; HV-05
|Priority|Must. Walking is the therapy; everything else supports it.

== Objective - Stay in the moment [OBJ-02] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-02
|Name|Stay in the moment
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|HFC-02, HFC-03. Sub-problems "Anchoring" (PS-01) and "Re-anchoring" (PS-04).
|Statement|During a walk or practice, the resident keeps place and purpose, or finds them again, without a person re-explaining.
|Type|Human-factors
|Derived from|HFC-02 Present-moment attention; HFC-03 Attention restoration
|Priority|Must.

== Objective - Welcome memories [OBJ-03] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-03
|Name|Welcome memories
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|HFC-04; VT-03. Woods et al. (2018).
|Statement|The walk invites memories the resident is glad to tell, and avoids those that hurt.
|Type|Value-derived
|Derived from|HV-08 Identity; bounded by VT-03
|Priority|Should.

== Objective - Calm at rest [OBJ-04] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-04
|Name|Calm at rest
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|HFC-02, HFC-05; PS-04, PS-05; goal on SA-06.
|Statement|Seated and lying practice, and evening listening, leave the resident calmer - without sedating medication as the default.
|Type|Human-factors
|Derived from|Goal on SA-06; HFC-02; HFC-05
|Priority|Should.

== Objective - Own choice [OBJ-05] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-05
|Name|Own choice
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|HV-01; Ryan & Deci (2000).
|Statement|The resident decides whether, what and how long. "No" is final for the moment.
|Type|Value-derived
|Derived from|HV-01 Autonomy
|Priority|Must.

== Objective - Adult voice [OBJ-06] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-06
|Name|Adult voice
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|HFC-06; VT-05. Williams et al. (2009); Kitwood (1997).
|Statement|Guidance never talks down: no elderspeak, no memory tests, no praise for the obvious.
|Type|Value-derived
|Derived from|HV-02 Dignity
|Priority|Should.

== Objective - Help without tracking [OBJ-07] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-07
|Name|Help without tracking
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|VT-01, VT-02; HFC-07. Niemeijer et al. (2010, 2015).
|Statement|When something goes wrong, a person arrives in time. No route or whereabouts are recorded.
|Type|Value-derived
|Derived from|HV-04 Safety; HV-03 Privacy
|Priority|Must.

== Objective - Time freed, company kept [OBJ-08] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-08
|Name|Time freed, company kept
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Goal on SA-02; VT-07.
|Statement|Staff spend less time per walk, and residents get no less human company.
|Type|Operational
|Derived from|Goal on SA-02; HV-06, HV-07
|Priority|Should. Never at the expense of OBJ-01 or of human company.

== Objective - Listening that fits [OBJ-09] ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|OBJ-09
|Name|Listening that fits
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|PS-06; HFC-05. Gerdner (2000).
|Statement|What plays fits the person, the hour and the mood, and the resident chose it.
|Type|Value-derived
|Derived from|HV-08 Identity; HV-01 Autonomy
|Priority|Could. Valuable, but walking comes first.

