= Use Case - Guided garden walk [UC01] =

**Report Format:** §2.3 Objectives, Use Cases, Functions, Premises and Claims

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|UC01
|Name|Guided garden walk
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Formalizes SA-01, SA-04, PS-01, PS-02 and DS-01. No primary data.
|Objective(s) served|OBJ-01, OBJ-02, OBJ-03, OBJ-05, OBJ-06, OBJ-07, OBJ-08
|TDP(s) and IDP(s) used|TDP-01; IDP-01, IDP-02, IDP-03
|Actors|(((
* ST-01 Resident (Direct) - walks, chooses, pauses
* ST-04 Walking partner, ST-07 Volunteer or ST-03 Family (Direct) - walks along, talks, presses pause
* ST-02 Care worker (Direct) - clips on the guide; receives alerts
* ST-08 Activity coordinator (Indirect) - wrote the profile; paired the walkers
* System - Pepper at the door (TECH-01), pocket guide (TECH-02), garden beacons (TECH-03), phone and record (TECH-04)
)))
|Trigger|Walk slot opens; or the resident asks to go out.
|Pre-condition|(((
* Resident assessed fit for the garden loop with a partner (ST-06); wider routes only with staff, volunteer or family
* Guide charged; beacons up; profile holds welcome and avoided topics
* Care worker reachable
* Consent arrangements in place (Open item O-8)
)))
|Post-condition|(((
Resident back inside, or a care worker has taken over after F4.

Record holds four items. No route, no words.
)))
|Action Sequence|(((
~1. Slot opens. Pepper at the door offers two options (F1, IDP-03).

~1-alt. Resident says no. Offer ends; no new offer within the configured interval.

~2. Resident agrees. Care worker clips on the guide; companion joins; care worker returns to the ward. Guide reports ready, or degraded (F4).

~3. Walk. Quiet start; then present-moment cues with long silences (F2, IDP-01).

~4. Landmark beacon: a place-bound cue, or a memory invitation from the profile; at most two invitations per walk (F2, IDP-02).

~5. Pause pressed by resident or companion: guide silent until pressed again.

~6. Stop at a bench: after a wait, offer of a short seated practice (F2).

~7. Hesitation, or a turn off the path: one orienting cue to something near (F2).

~8. Gate beacon: one orienting cue back; alert to the care worker (F4). **Deliberate addition.**

~9. Pull-cord, fall-like impact, or no movement and no press after two check-ins: alert (F4). Guide tells the resident someone is coming.

~10. Set time reached: head-back cue towards the door (F2).

~11. At the door, Pepper welcomes back with one statement about the walk (F2). **Deliberate addition** - re-exposure to the walk (HFC-01).

~12. F5 records the session.

**Exception.** Guide silent, flat, or unable to send alerts: the walk goes on as today, with the companion, on the garden loop only. Degraded state shown at step 2. Verified by UC01-F4-PR4.
)))
|Function(s) realized|F1, F2, F4, F5

= Use Case - Seated or lying practice [UC02] =

**Report Format:** §2.3 Objectives, Use Cases, Functions, Premises and Claims

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|UC02
|Name|Seated or lying practice
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Formalizes SA-05, SA-06, PS-03, PS-04, PS-05, DS-02 and DS-03. No primary data.
|Objective(s) served|OBJ-02, OBJ-04, OBJ-05, OBJ-06, OBJ-07
|TDP(s) and IDP(s) used|TDP-01; IDP-01, IDP-03
|Actors|(((
* ST-01 Resident (Direct) - sits or lies; pauses or stops
* ST-08 Activity coordinator (Direct) - starts lounge sessions
* ST-02 Care worker (Direct) - starts bedside practice at dusk
* System - Pepper in the lounge (TECH-01); pocket guide docked at the bedside (TECH-02)
)))
|Trigger|Rain-day slot; after a walk; restlessness at dusk; the resident asks.
|Pre-condition|Resident agreed. Pepper in the lounge, or guide docked at the bedside. Staff reachable.
|Post-condition|Practice ended by the resident or at the set time. May continue into listening (UC03). Session recorded.
|Action Sequence|(((
~1. Offer (F1): sit or lie with the voice, or not now.

~1-alt. No: offer ends.

~2. Opening: posture cue - chair, pillow. Breathing light (Pepper only).

~3. Cues: body, breath, sound. Concrete; no imagery. Long silences (F3, IDP-01).

~4. Resident speaks, presses or touches: pause. "Stop": end.

~5. Cues return at intervals; each one is a way back in. No drift sensing.

~6. Set time: a short close, no praise. Offer of listening (UC03) or quiet (F1).

~7. F5 records the session.

**Exception.** Pepper unavailable: the docked guide, voice only. No device: as today (SA-05, SA-06).
)))
|Function(s) realized|F1, F3, F5

= Use Case - Listening [UC03] =

**Report Format:** §2.3 Objectives, Use Cases, Functions, Premises and Claims

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|UC03
|Name|Listening: radio, news, audiobooks
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Formalizes SA-07, PS-05, PS-06, DS-02 and DS-03. No primary data.
|Objective(s) served|OBJ-04, OBJ-05, OBJ-09
|TDP(s) and IDP(s) used|IDP-03
|Actors|(((
* ST-01 Resident (Direct) - chooses, changes, stops
* ST-08 Activity coordinator, ST-03 Family (Indirect) - write and correct the profile
* System - library and recommender (TECH-05), through Pepper or the docked guide
)))
|Trigger|After practice; at rest; the resident asks.
|Pre-condition|Profile written with family. Library loaded. News source chosen (Open item O-6).
|Post-condition|Resident listened, changed or stopped. Liked or skipped noted per item. No listening log.
|Action Sequence|(((
~1. Offer two items, by hour, state and profile (F6, IDP-03).

~2. Resident picks one, asks for something else, or says no.

~3. Long book: a one-line recap first. Short stories preferred.

~4. "News", at any hour: the news plays, in one step. Evening: calm content offered first; news never hidden.

~5. "Stop" or "another": stops; item marked skipped.

~6. Item ends, or set time: fade out in the evening.

~7. F5 records type and minutes; no titles.

**Exception.** Recommender down: the two standing favourites from the profile.
)))
|Function(s) realized|F6, F5

= Functions =

**F1 Invite.** At the slot, or on request: offer two options; accept any answer. "No" ends the offer; no new offer within the configured interval. Serves OBJ-01, OBJ-05, OBJ-08. Bounded by VT-07. Enabled by TECH-01 (door, lounge), TECH-02 (bedside).

**F2 Guide the walk.** Present-moment cues with long silences (IDP-01). Place-bound cues and memory invitations at landmarks (IDP-02), from a prepared script and the life-story profile - never generated on the spot. Short seated practice at a bench. One orienting cue at a hesitation or the gate. Head-back cue at the set time. Welcome back at the door. Pause on the button. Serves OBJ-01, OBJ-02, OBJ-03, OBJ-06, OBJ-08. Bounded by VT-01, VT-03, VT-05, VT-06, VT-07. Enabled by TECH-02, TECH-03; TECH-01 at the door.

**F3 Guide seated and lying practice.** Body, breath, sound. Concrete; no imagery. Long silences; breathing light. Pauses on speech, touch or button; ends on "stop" or at the set time. Serves OBJ-02, OBJ-04, OBJ-05, OBJ-06. Bounded by VT-05. Enabled by TECH-01 (lounge), TECH-02 (docked).

**F4 Call a person.** Alert the care worker on pull-cord, gate, fall-like impact, or no movement and no press after two check-ins. Send resident, trigger, last landmark - nothing more. Tell the resident someone is coming. Report a degraded state at the start of a walk. Serves OBJ-07, OBJ-08. Bounded by VT-01, VT-02. Enabled by TECH-02, TECH-03, TECH-04.

**F5 Keep a short record.** Per session: type, minutes, ended early, person called and reason. No route, no words, no titles. Serves OBJ-07, OBJ-08. Bounded by VT-02, VT-06. Enabled by TECH-04.

**F6 Recommend listening.** Offer two items by hour, state and profile. One-line recap for long books. Evening default: calm content. News on request, any hour, in one step - never hidden. Learns only liked or skipped. Serves OBJ-04, OBJ-05, OBJ-09. Bounded by VT-04, VT-06. Enabled by TECH-05, through TECH-01 or TECH-02.

//Why memory invitations are prepared, not generated. A generated line can state a wrong fact about a person's own life, which violates HV-08 more than silence would. Prepared lines are checked by family and ST-08 (Open item O-5).//

= Premises =

Verification only: does the Function work as specified.

|=Premise ID|=Function|=Evaluation Method(s) / Measure(s)|=Verification Criteria|=Step(s)
|UC01-F1-PR1|F1|EM-01; M-01. No human subjects.|Takes no for an answer. No new offer within [threshold - O-3] of a "no". Never more than two options. Nothing starts before a yes.|UC01 1, 1-alt; UC02 1
|UC01-F2-PR2|F2|EM-01; M-01. No human subjects.|Silence share at least [threshold - O-3]. Landmark cue within [threshold - O-3] s of the beacon; stop detected within [threshold - O-3] s. At most two memory invitations per walk; none from avoided topics. Pause takes effect within 1 s.|UC01 3-7, 10
|UC02-F3-PR3|F3|EM-01; M-01. No human subjects.|Pauses within [threshold - O-3] s of speech, press or touch. "Stop" ends the session. Never runs past the set time. Script contains no imagery (script check).|UC02 2-6
|UC01-F4-PR4|F4|EM-01; M-01. No human subjects.|Gate, pull-cord, impact and no-response events reach the phone within [threshold - O-3] s. Alert carries resident, trigger, last landmark only. No location stored. Unacknowledged alerts escalate. Degraded state reported at start.|UC01 2, 8, 9
|UC01-F5-PR5|F5|EM-01; M-08 (content check). No human subjects.|Record holds exactly: type, minutes, ended early, person called and reason. No route, no words, no titles.|UC01 12; UC02 7; UC03 7
|UC03-F6-PR6|F6|EM-01; M-01, M-08 (content check). No human subjects.|Never plays without a choice. Two options per offer. Evening rule applied. "News" plays within one step at any hour. Profile holds only its listed fields and liked/skipped; resident and family can see and correct it (via ST-08).|UC03 1-5

= Claims =

Validation: does the Function have the intended effect. Claim numbers are project-wide.

|=Claim ID|=Function|=Serves Objective|=Effect|=Grounding|=Evaluation Method(s) / Measure(s)|=Validation Criteria|=Step(s)
|UC01-F1-CL1|F1|OBJ-01, OBJ-05|Positive. A two-option invitation at the door increases walks started, compared with staff suggestion alone. Concerns ST-01, SA-01, PS-02.|HV-01; Ryan & Deci (2000).|EM-02; M-02, M-07|Walks started per week above the resident's baseline; M-07 observer score no lower.|1
|UC01-F2-CL2|F2|OBJ-01, OBJ-02|Positive. Present-moment cues reduce early turn-backs and lengthen walks, without more distress. Concerns ST-01, SA-01, PS-01.|HFC-02, HFC-03; Churcher Clarke et al. (2017); Kaplan (1995).|EM-02; M-02, M-05, M-04|Fewer walks ended early; more minutes per walk; M-04 negative affect no higher.|3, 6, 7
|UC01-F2-CL3|F2|OBJ-01|Positive. Events on a guided walk are recalled better the same day than matched events in a seated session. Concerns ST-01.|HFC-01 (hypothesis); Chrastil & Warren (2012); Erickson et al. (2011); Engelkamp (1998).|EM-02; M-03|Recall and recognition higher for walk events, within resident. A null result weakens the walking-first argument and is reported as such.|3, 4, 11
|UC01-F2-CL4|F2|OBJ-03|Positive. Memory invitations at landmarks raise engagement, pleasure and talk between partners. Concerns ST-01, ST-04, SA-04, PS-02.|HFC-04; Woods et al. (2018).|EM-02; M-05, M-04|M-05 and M-04 pleasure higher on walks with invitations than without.|4
|UC01-F2-CL5|F2|OBJ-03, OBJ-07|**Adverse.** Memory invitations stir longing for the former home: more gate alerts, more sadness. Concerns ST-01, PS-01.|HFC-04; VT-03.|EM-02; M-04; gate alerts (F5 record)|Holds if gate alerts per walk or M-04 sadness rise on walks with invitations. If it holds: invitations only at the bench, or only for residents they suit.|4, 8
|UC01-F2-CL6|F2, F3|OBJ-06|**Adverse.** The guide's voice is heard as talking down. Concerns ST-01, HV-02.|HFC-06, HFC-08; VT-05; Williams et al. (2009).|EM-04, EM-02, EM-03; M-08 (code T), M-04|Holds if residents or staff call the voice childish or condescending (code T), or M-04 anger rises. If it holds: rewrite in EM-04 before EM-02 goes on.|3, 4; UC02 3
|UC01-F4-CL7|F4|OBJ-07|Positive. Alerts bring a person in time, and the resident does not feel tracked. Concerns ST-01, ST-02, HV-03, HV-04.|HFC-07; VT-02; Niemeijer et al. (2015).|EM-01, EM-02, EM-03; M-01, M-08 (W, R)|Alert latency within PR4's threshold in real use; no W or R codes from residents; staff judge alerts proportionate.|8, 9
|UC01-F2-CL8|F2|OBJ-08|Positive. Staff minutes per walk fall, and human company does not. Concerns ST-02, ST-01, HV-06, HV-07.|VT-07.|EM-02, EM-03; M-09, M-10, M-02|M-09 below baseline, and M-10 not below baseline, and walks (M-02) not fewer. Time saved by cutting company does not count.|2
|UC02-F3-CL9|F3|OBJ-02, OBJ-04|Positive. Concrete, paced practice holds engagement longer than a recorded relaxation exercise. Concerns ST-01, ST-08, SA-05, PS-04.|HFC-02; Churcher Clarke et al. (2017).|EM-02; M-05, M-04|M-05 engagement longer than with the home's usual recording; M-04 anxiety no higher.|UC02 2-5
|UC02-F3-CL10|F3|OBJ-04|Positive. Lying practice at dusk lowers evening agitation. Concerns ST-01, ST-02, SA-06, PS-05.|HFC-02; Khachiyants et al. (2011).|EM-02; M-06; PRN doses (secondary)|CMAI evening behaviours below baseline. PRN doses reported, not a criterion: ST-06 decides on medication.|UC02 1-6
|UC02-F3-CL11|F3|OBJ-07|**Adverse.** A device leading practice in the room is felt as being watched. Concerns ST-01, HV-03.|HFC-07, HFC-08; Pemberton et al. (2026).|EM-02, EM-03; M-08 (W)|Holds if residents describe Pepper or the docked guide as watching or checking (code W). If it holds for Pepper: guide alone, voice only.|UC02 2-5
|UC03-F6-CL12|F6|OBJ-09|Positive. Personalised two-option offers are accepted more often, and kept on longer, than the default station. Concerns ST-01, SA-07, PS-06.|HFC-05, HFC-04; Gerdner (2000); Thomas et al. (2017).|EM-02; M-11, M-04|Acceptance and minutes above the default-station baseline; M-04 pleasure no lower.|UC03 1-2
|UC03-F6-CL13|F6|OBJ-04, OBJ-09|Positive. Calm content as the evening default lowers evening distress. Concerns ST-01, SA-06, PS-05.|HFC-05; VT-04.|EM-02; M-06, M-04|CMAI evening behaviours and M-04 anxiety below baseline.|UC03 1, 4
|UC03-F6-CL14|F6|OBJ-05, OBJ-09|**Adverse.** The evening default is felt as being kept from the news. Concerns ST-01, ST-03, HV-01.|VT-04; HV-01, HV-02.|EM-02, EM-03; M-08 (code K), M-07|Holds if residents or family describe being kept from the news (code K), or M-07 falls. If it holds: news offered first, at every hour.|UC03 4

