= Open items =

|=ID|=Item|=Blocks|=Owner
|O-1|No primary data. All references cited from memory: evidence pass to check each one against its source.|Every Evidence basis|Group
|O-2|Walking and memory (HFC-01) rests on a group observation: holiday moments on foot are remembered better than moments sitting down. Find a direct source; until then, a hypothesis that UC01-F2-CL3 tests.|HFC-01; CL3|Group
|O-3|Thresholds for PR1 to PR6: silence share, cue latency, stop detection, alert latency, re-offer interval. Set from an EM-01 pilot and care-worker input.|PR1 to PR6|Group
|O-4|Hearing: speaker audible to resident and partner outdoors, with hearing aids, wind and traffic. Test in EM-04.|TECH-02; F2|Group
|O-5|Life-story profile: who writes it, how often it is reviewed, how avoided topics are found. Form for ST-08 and families.|F2, F6; VT-03, VT-06|ST-08 with group
|O-6|News source: plain-language, accurate, licensed. No unchecked generated summaries.|F6; UC03|Group
|O-7|Garden policy with ST-05 and ST-06: who may walk the loop with a partner instead of staff; who answers a gate alert.|UC01 pre-condition; VT-01|ST-05, ST-06
|O-8|Consent and data: lawful basis (GDPR), supported consent, representative, where profile and records are stored.|UC01 to UC03 pre-conditions; VT-02, VT-06|ST-05
|O-9|Pepper indoors: room by the lounge window and the garden door; not in bedrooms (docked guide instead). Check on site.|TECH-01; RP-01|Group

